{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeshjaBxaGB33JR7j3VGt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Now I'll move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values; add `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to the Order data class.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add `findByStatus(status: OrderStatus): List<Shipment>` method and a helper `update(order: Order)` method to allow updating an existing order's status.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for a given order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist (404)\n   - Checks if any shipment has CONFIRMED status; if so, throws ConflictException (409) and changes nothing\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, succeeds without changes (idempotent)\n   - If order is ACTIVE, changes all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED and changes order to CANCELLED\n   - Returns the cancelled order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: Update the create method to check if the order exists and is CANCELLED; if so, throw ConflictException (409).\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add error codes `ORDER_CANCELLED` (or similar) if needed, or reuse `CONFLICT` for the \"can't create shipment for cancelled order\" case.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add comprehensive tests covering all the cancel scenarios mentioned in the ticket.\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered whether to make order cancellation transactional at the database level, but since this is an in-memory store with ConcurrentHashMap, I'll use a simple pattern: check all shipments first (atomic read), validate the conditions, then apply all changes (atomic writes). The \"all-or-nothing\" requirement is satisfied by not persisting any changes if validation fails.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Happy path - ACTIVE → CANCELLED**: \n  - Read order by ID → throws 404 if not found\n  - Read all shipments for order → check for CONFIRMED status → throw 409 if found (no changes)\n  - Update order status to CANCELLED\n  - Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n  - Return updated order\n\n- **Idempotent re-cancel**:\n  - Read order → throw 404 if not found\n  - Check all shipments for CONFIRMED status → throw 409 if found\n  - Order is already CANCELLED → succeed, return as-is\n\n- **Blocked by CONFIRMED shipment**:\n  - Read order → throw 404 if not found\n  - Read shipments → find CONFIRMED → throw 409, no changes to order or shipments\n\n- **Create shipment on CANCELLED order**:\n  - Read order → throw 404 (existing behavior)\n  - If order exists and status is CANCELLED → throw 409 with new error code\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancel_active_order_succeeds_and_cancels_created_shipments` - Cancel an ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments\n2. `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotently` - Repeated cancel succeeds\n3. `cancel_fails_409_when_shipment_confirmed_and_changes_nothing` - CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel\n4. `cancel_fails_404_for_unknown_order` - Non-existent order\n5. `create_shipment_fails_409_when_order_cancelled` - Creating shipment for cancelled order\n\nNow I'll implement:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_read_input_tokens":20448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":319},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b4d64d8-c1fe-478a-a134-a19719902463","uuid":"cf4851a6-4450-47e4-9082